m_stands\",\"snap_ebt_markets\",\"snap_ebt_pct\",\"organic_vendor_markets\",\"organic_pct\",\"markets_with_website\",\"website_pct\"\n\"California\",\"CA\",647,95,223,100,15.5,114,17.6,246,38.0\n\"New York\",\"NY\",555,156,272,41,7.4,45,8.1,283,51.0\n\"Pennsylvania\",\"PA\",426,102,886,18,4.2,43,10.1,226,53.1\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786915090309},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good, I can see the farmers markets data by state. Now let me look at the census data to see what's there and identify the US total row.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_0178BkF9Wb2LiJxedbXLhSft","name":"xorq_select","arguments":{"catalog_path":".xorq/catalog","on":"census","compose":"source.select(\"SUMLEV\", \"NAME\", \"POPESTIMATE2025\").limit(10)"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":13,"output":158,"cacheRead":17238,"cacheWrite":415,"totalTokens":17824,"cost":{"input":0.000013,"output":0.00079,"cacheRead":0.0017238000000000002,"cacheWrite":0.00051875,"total":0.00304555},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":37},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786915090309,"responseId":"msg_011Ce789Dv6QfpQwgXKKhyJs","rawStopReason":"tool_use"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_0178BkF9Wb2LiJxedbXLhSft","toolName":"xorq_select","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\"SUMLEV\",\"NAME\",\"POPESTIMATE2025\"\n10,\"United States\",341784857\n20,\"Northeast Region\",58042054\n30,\"New England\",15431980\n30,\"Middle Atlantic\",42610074\n20,\"Midwest Region\",69762666\n30,\"East North Central\",47693655\n30,\"West North Central\",22069011\n20,\"South Region\",133833983\n30,\"South Atlantic\",70198706\n30,\"East South Central\",20069188\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786915093780},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Perfect! I can see:\n- SUMLEV=10 is the US total (\"United States\")\n- The 2025 population estimate is 341,784,857\n\nNow I need to:\n1. Get the total number of farmers markets from the farmers_markets table\n2. Use the 2025 population (341,784,857)\n3. Calculate: (total farmers markets / 341,784,857) * 100,000\n\nLet me first get the total number of farmers markets by summing the farmers_markets column.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01CLkk4XfcS9HffVaZe11qjK","name":"xorq_select","arguments":{"catalog_path":".xorq/catalog","on":"farmers_markets","compose":"source.aggregate(total_markets=source.farmers_markets.sum())"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":13,"output":241,"cacheRead":17653,"cacheWrite":286,"totalTokens":18193,"cost":{"input":0.000013,"output":0.0012050000000000001,"cacheRead":0.0017653000000000002,"cacheWrite":0.0003575,"total":0.0033408000000000005},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":125},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786915093780,"responseId":"msg_011Ce789TF2np3VWXtQ7Q7Yr","rawStopReason":"tool_use"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01CLkk4XfcS9HffVaZe11qjK","toolName":"xorq_select","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\"total_markets\"\n7944\n\n(showing up to 50 rows; pass limit or aggregate to count — do not page)"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786915097122},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Great! So there are 7,944 farmers markets total in the dataset. Now I need to get the US population from the census data and create the metric. Let me use xorq_select to directly get the per-capita value.\n\nActually, the best approach would be to create a single build script that reads both datasets, joins them (with a constant key since one is a total and the other is by-state totals), and computes the metric. But looking at the census data, I should sum the farmers markets data to get the total, and use the US population (SUMLEV=10) to compute the rate.\n\nWait, let me re-read the farmers markets schema. It looks like it has state rows, not a US total. So I need to:\n1. Sum all farmers markets from the state-level data\n2. Use the US total population from the census data\n3. Calculate the rate\n\nLet me create a build script that does this join and calculation.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Now I'll create a build script that combines both datasets to calculate the metric:"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01ViV1Kq3AGFM3KnfQssY7oW","name":"write","arguments":{"path":".xorq/scripts/build_farmers_markets_per_capita.py","content":"import urllib.request as u\n_o = u.build_opener()\n_o.addheaders = [(\"User-Agent\", \"Mozilla/5.0\")]\nu.install_opener(_o)\n\nfrom xorq.vendor.ibis.common.collections import FrozenDict\nimport xorq.api as xo\n\nso = FrozenDict({\"User-Agent\": \"Mozilla/5.0\"})\ncon = xo.pandas.connect()\n\n# Read farmers markets by state\nfact = xo.deferred_read_csv(\n    \"https://harvestlymarkets.com/data/us-farmers-markets-by-state-2026.csv\",\n    con,\n    table_name=\"farmers_markets\",\n    storage_options=so,\n)\n\n# Read census data\nref = xo.deferred_read_csv(\n    \"https://gist.githubusercontent.com/hussainsultan/369600f5179b22792a2b4c9ed37de056/raw/NST-EST2025-ALLDATA.csv\",\n    con,\n    table_name=\"census\",\n    storage_options=so,\n)\n\n# Aggregate farmers markets to get US total\ntotals = fact.aggregate(total_markets=fact.farmers_markets.sum()).mutate(k=xo.literal(1))\n\n# Get US population from census (SUMLEV=10 is the US total)\nus_pop = (ref.filter(ref.SUMLEV == 10)\n          .select(\"POPESTIMATE2025\").mutate(k=xo.literal(1)))\n\n# Join and calculate per 100k\nexpr = (\n    totals.join(us_pop, totals.k == us_pop.k)\n      .mutate(markets_per_100k=totals.total_markets / us_pop.POPESTIMATE2025 * 100000)\n      .select(\"total_markets\", \"POPESTIMATE2025\", \"markets_per_100k\")\n)\n"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":12,"output":797,"cacheRead":17939,"cacheWrite":288,"totalTokens":19036,"cost":{"input":0.000012,"output":0.003985000000000001,"cacheRead":0.0017939000000000002,"cacheWrite":0.00036,"total":0.006150900000000001},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":216},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786915097122,"responseId":"msg_011Ce789mkX4SXdJp7k686gW","rawStopReason":"tool_use"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01ViV1Kq3AGFM3KnfQssY7oW","toolName":"write","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully wrote 1250 bytes to .xorq/scripts/build_farmers_markets_per_capita.py"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786915105752},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now let me build this script and add it to the catalog.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01DrkWyFsUXjRuzffYe7hn2r","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /private/tmp/trial-pi-67-z_3s7ex5 && xorq build .xorq/scripts/build_farmers_markets_per_capita.py --builds-dir .xorq/builds --emit-build-path-to /tmp/bp_metric.txt && cat /tmp/bp_metric.txt"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":13,"output":151,"cacheRead":18227,"cacheWrite":841,"totalTokens":19232,"cost":{"input":0.000013,"output":0.000755,"cacheRead":0.0018227000000000002,"cacheWrite":0.00105125,"total":0.0036419500000000006},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":18},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786915105753,"responseId":"msg_011Ce78APVqPPQKjVvJyWH2F","rawStopReason":"tool_use"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01DrkWyFsUXjRuzffYe7hn2r","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Building expr from .xorq/scripts/build_farmers_markets_per_capita.py\n/nix/store/yvlv6n4rx6dnnvhi7sgc5lm0152pa8mx-pi-xorq-duel-dev-env/lib/python3.13/site-packages/xorq/ibis_yaml/sql.py:120: UserWarning: <xorq.backends.pandas.Backend object at 0x12b8e3490> is not a SQL backend, so no SQL string will be generated\n  \"sql\": to_sql(expr).strip(),\nWritten 'expr' to .xorq/builds/79cf94a2e30a\n.xorq/builds/79cf94a2e30a\n.xorq/builds/79cf94a2e30a"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786915109394},{"role":"